## Real-Time Event Flow

````carousel
```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant P1 as Player 1
    participant SIO as Socket.IO Server
    participant DB as Database
    participant P2 as Player 2

    P1->>SIO: join_match {match_id}
    SIO->>DB: Load match + challenge
    SIO-->>P1: MATCH_FOUND {challenge, players}

    P2->>SIO: join_match {match_id}
    SIO-->>P1: MATCH_START {time_limit}
    SIO-->>P2: MATCH_START {time_limit}
    SIO-->>P1: TIMER_START {600s}
    SIO-->>P2: TIMER_START {600s}

    loop Every 5s
        SIO-->>P1: TIMER_TICK {elapsed, remaining}
        SIO-->>P2: TIMER_TICK {elapsed, remaining}
    end

    P1->>SIO: submit_solution {code}
    SIO->>DB: Save + evaluate
    SIO-->>P2: PLAYER_SUBMISSION
    SIO-->>P1: SCORE_UPDATE {80, 0}
    SIO-->>P1: judge_result {score, feedback}

    P2->>SIO: submit_solution {code}
    SIO->>DB: Finalize match, update MMR+XP
    SIO-->>P1: MATCH_END {winner, xp, mmr}
    SIO-->>P2: MATCH_END {winner, xp, mmr}
```
<!-- slide -->
```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant P1 as Player 1
    participant SIO as Socket.IO Server
    participant DB as Database

    P1-xSIO: disconnect
    SIO-->>P2: PLAYER_DISCONNECTED {grace: 30s}

    Note over SIO: 30s grace timer running

    P1->>SIO: join_match (reconnect)
    SIO->>SIO: Cancel grace timer
    SIO-->>P2: PLAYER_RECONNECTED

    Note over SIO: Timer expired (forfeit path)
    SIO->>DB: Finalize - opponent wins
    SIO-->>P2: FORFEIT + MATCH_END
```
````

---

## API Endpoints Summary

| Method | Path | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| POST | `/pvp/queue/join` | Join matchmaking, instantly matches if opponent found |
| POST | `/pvp/queue/leave` | Leave queue |
| GET | `/pvp/match/status/{user_id}` | Poll for match status (3s interval) |
| GET | `/pvp/match/{match_id}` | Full match details |
| POST | `/pvp/match/{match_id}/submit` | REST-based code/answer submission |
| POST | `/pvp/match/{match_id}/forfeit` | Forfeit match |
| GET | `/pvp/history/{user_id}` | Paginated battle history |
| GET | `/pvp/status` | Authenticated user's real PvP stats |
| GET | `/pvp/rating/{user_id}` | Any user's MMR rating |
| GET | `/pvp/leaderboard` | MMR-ranked global leaderboard |
| GET | `/pvp/matches/live` | Currently in-progress matches |

---

## Verification Notes

To test the full system:

1. **Start backend:** `uvicorn main:app --reload` in `/backend`
2. **Start frontend:** `npm run dev` in project root
3. **Log in** with two separate accounts (different browsers/incognito)
4. **Both click "Find Match"** — one will wait, the second triggers an instant match
5. **Watch for:** Socket.IO connection, MATCH_FOUND event, timer countdown, live score update, MATCH_END result screen with XP/MMR values
6. **Leaderboard / Hero stats** — after first match, will show real data instead of Novice defaults

> [!NOTE]
> On first run, `Base.metadata.create_all()` in `main.py` creates all 5 new tables automatically. No manual migration needed in dev.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The `judging.py` `AIJudge` class uses simulated scoring. For production, replace `evaluate_submission` with an LLM API call (GPT-4, Claude) that analyzes the submitted code against the challenge spec.
